<title>ISRAEL: Israel grain, meal, soy arrivals detailed.</title>
<headline>Israel grain, meal, soy arrivals detailed.</headline>
<dateline>TEL AVIV 1997-01-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following shipments of grain have arrived or are due to arrive in Israeli ports, according to the inspection agency Hevra Klalit Lehashgaha (in tonnes):</p>
<p>Vessel	     ETA	   Cargo	    Quantity   Origin</p>
<p>Fany		 unloading   corn	     21,733     U.S.</p>
<p>				     soya		8,976</p>
<p>				     wheat	     9,081</p>
<p>Nicolay	    unloading   rapeseed meal   4,522     India</p>
<p>Dobrelybov</p>
<p>Polinova	   unloading   sunflower meal  1,500     Europe</p>
<p>Bodaybo	    unloading   sunflower seed  1,849     Europe</p>
<p>Unity		01/01	 sorghum	  10,500     U.S.</p>
<p>				     corn	     22,000</p>
<p>				     corn-gluten    11,300</p>
<p>				     corn-screening  6,500</p>
<p>Lake Tahoe	 arrived     barley	   19,023     U.S.</p>
<p>Sac Malaga	 arrived     barley	   23,742     U.S.</p>
<p>City of Chios    07/01	 maize grits     2,600     Europe</p>
<p>Vlas Chubar	08/01	 soya		  450     Europe</p>
<p>				     barley	    1,553</p>
<p>n/a		  10/01	 feed wheat	3,000     Europe</p>
<p>Davuti	     15/01	 sunflower meal  1,500     Europe</p>
<p>Naki		 18/01	 n/a		70,000     U.S.</p>
<p>n/a		  20/01	 bran		2,000     Europe</p>
<p>Southern Venture 24/01	 wheat	    43,000     U.S.</p>
<p>				     sorghum</p>
<p>Solidarnosk	30/01	 soya	     13,000     U.S.</p>
<p>				     corn+sorghum   47,000</p>
<p>Vera		 03/02	 wheat	    30,000     U.S.</p>
<p>				     sorghum</p>
<p>Spiridon	   n/a	   sorghum, wheat    n/a     U.S.</p>
